{"availability":"available","full":"mariotristan/planets","name":"planets","description":"🚀 Astronaut Bruno Tristan's Planet Explorer — a kids' (ages 6–8) solar system app in English and Spanish: orbiting planets, size and weight comparisons, rocket trips, a quiz and stickers. Plain HTML/CSS/JS, works offline.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-04T05:42:08Z","updated":"2026-10-11T06:02:53Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://mariotristan.github.io/planets/","topics":["astronomy","bilingual","education","kids","offline-first","planets","pwa","solar-system","spanish","vanilla-js"],"demo":"https://mariotristan.github.io/planets/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T18:52:23.730Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T18:52:23.730Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T18:52:23.730Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T14:52:51.381Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T18:52:23.730Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An interactive website that teaches young kids (ages 6–8) about the Sun, the 8 planets, the Moon and Pluto, guided by Astronaut Bruno. It works on tablets (touch) and computers (mouse), in English and Spanish."],"features":["🪐 Explore: The planets orbit the Sun, the Moon circles Earth, and Pluto has its own dotted orbit. Tap any body to open a fact card with short facts and a 🔊 read-aloud button.","⚖️ Compare: See two bodies side by side at their true relative size, and slide to find out how much you'd weigh on each one.","🚀 Fly: Pick a destination and watch Bruno's rocket fly there from Earth. See how far away it is and how long the trip would take by walking, car, airplane and rocket.","❓ Quiz: 8 random questions per round from a bank of 30. Earn a ⭐ for each first-try answer; your best score is saved.","🏅 Stickers: Collect a stamp for every body you visit, plus badges for the quiz, Compare and Fly tabs."],"sourceUrl":"https: